      "content": "Thanks, that's a solid start and the flow feels pretty natural. You managed to get all the keywords in there without it feeling too forced. \n\nHowever, I just checked the internal dashboard for our submission preview, and it shows the current keyword density is actually quite low because some of the terms are only used once. The automated screener is pretty strict—if we don't hit a higher density, we might get filtered out before a human even sees it. \n\nCould you expand this into a more detailed three-paragraph summary? We need more depth on the actual field implementation. Just please, try to keep it sounding professional and avoid making it look like a list; I really don't want the reviewers to think we're just gaming the system, even if we do need to make sure those specific terms are prominent throughout the text.",
